# 000300-000399/20070124T205313Z_102981737.wiki
zΔ⚡b|=2ee|+The diff utility was developed in the early 1970s on the [[Unix]] operating system which was emerging from [[|=1|+T&T]] [[Bell Labs]] in Murray|=1|+Hill, New Jersey.%0AThe final version, first shipped with the 5th E|=2|+tion o|=1|+ Unix in 1974, was entirely written by [[Douglas McIlroy]].%0AThis research was published in a 1976 paper co%2Dwritten with [[James W. Hunt]] who developed an initial prototype o|=2|+d|=1|+ff.%0A%0AMcIlroy'|=2|+work wa|=1|+ preceded and inf|=1|+uenced by [[Stephen C. Johnson%7CSteve Johnson]]'s comp|=1|+riso|=1|+ pro|=1|+ram|=1|+on [[GECOS]] and [[Mike Lesk]]'s '''proo|=1|+''' pr|=1|+g|=1|+am.%0A'''Proof'''|=1|-1|+originate|=1|+ on Un|=1|+x and |=1|+roduced line%2Dby%2Dline changes|=1|+like di|=1|+f and even |=1|+sed angle%2Dbra|=2|+ets (">|=2|+and "<") for presenting line insertions and deletions in the program's output.%0AThe [[heuristi|=1|+]]s used in these ear|=1|+y applicati|=1|+n|=1|+ were, however, deemed unr|=2|+iable.%0AThe potential usefulness of a diff tool provoked McIlro|=2|+into rese|=1|+rching and de|=1|+igning a more robu|=1|+t t|=1|+ol that |=1|+ould be used |=1|+n a v|=1|+rie|=1|+y of tasks but p|=1|+rform well in the processing an|=2|+space limitations of the [[PDP%2D11]]'s hardware.%0AHis approach resulted from collaboration also |=5|+individuals a|=1|+ Bell Labs including [[Alfred A|=1|+o]], [[Elliot Pinson]], [[J|=1|+ffrey|=1|+Ullman]], and [[Harold S. Stone]].%0A%0AIn the con|=2|+xt of Unix, the use of the [[Ed (Unix)%7Ced]] line edito|=1|+ provided diff with the natural ability to create |=1|+achine%2Dusable|=2|+e|=2|+t scri|=1|+ts".%0AThese edit|=2|+cripts, w|=1|+en saved to a file, can, along w|=2|-1|+h the original file, be reconstituted by '''ed''' into the modified file in its entirety.%0AThis greatly reduced|=3|+e sp|=1|+ce necessary |=1|+o maintain|=1|+multiple versi|=1|+ns of a file.%0AMcIl|=1|+oy cons|=1|+dered writin|=1|+ a post%2Dprocessor for d|=1|+ff where a variety of output formats could be desig|=1|+ed |=1|+nd implemen|=3|+, but he found|=2|+t more frugal a|=1|+d|=1|-1|+simpler to have diff be responsible for generating the syntax and reverse%2Dord|=1|+r i|=1|+pu|=1|+ accepted by the '''ed''' c|=1|+mmand. I|=1|+ 1985|=2|+[[Larry |=2|+ll]] compo|=1|+ed a separate utility, [[patc|=1|+ (Unix)%7Cpatch]], that generalized and extended the ability to modify files with diff output.%0A%0AIn diff's early years, common uses included compar|=3|+ changes in |=1|+he s|=1|+urce of software code a|=1|+d markup for technical documents, verifying program debugging output, comparing filesystem listings and analyzing computer assembly code.%0AThe output targeted for '''ed''' was motivated to provide compression for a sequence of modifications made to a file.%0AThe [[SCCS%7CSource Code Control System]] (SCCS) emerged in the late 1970s as a direct consequence of this development.%0A%0AA conceptual predecessor of diff includes [[Project Xanadu]], a hypertext project established in 1960 that had envisioned a version tracking system necessary for its "transpointing windows" feature.%0AAs part of this feature, file differences were subsumed in the expansive term "[[transclusion]]", when a document has included in it parts of other documents or revisions.%0A%0AIn the digital realm of the humanities, computer comparison systems were understood to have been created for working on literary works published as large volumes.|=3b69|
