# 000300-000399/20070327T041845Z_118185041.wiki
zΔ⚡b|=2ee|-1|+The d|=4|+ut|=1|+lity wa|=2|+developed in the e|=1|+rly 1970s on|=2|+he [[Unix]] op|=2|+ating syste|=2|+which was emerging from [[AT&T]] [[Bell Labs]] in M|=1|+rray Hill, New Jer|=2|+y.%0AThe final version, first shippe|=2|+w|=1|+th the 5th Editio|=2|-1|+of Unix in 1974, was |=3|+irely written by [[D|=1|+uglas McIlroy]].%0AThis research was published i|=2|+a 1976 paper co%2Dwritten with [[James |=1|+. Hunt]] who developed |=1|+n initial prototype of diff.%0A%0AMcIlroy'|=1|+ work was preceded and influenced by [[Step|=1|+en C. Johnson%7CSteve Johnson]]'s compar|=1|+so|=1|+ pro|=1|+ram on [[GECOS]] and [[Mike Lesk]]'s <|=1|+t>proof</tt> program.%0A<tt>proof</tt> also originated |=3|+Unix and, like diff, produced line%2Dby%2Dline changes and even used angle%2Dbrackets (">" and "<") for presenting line insertions and deletions in |=2|+e progr|=1|+m's ou|=1|+put.%0AThe|=1|+[[heur|=2|+tic]]s used|=1|+in t|=1|+ese early appl|=1|+cations were, however, deemed unreliable.%0AThe potential usefulness of a diff tool provoked McIlroy into researchin|=1|+ and designing a more robust tool t|=1|+at cou|=1|+d be used in a variet|=4|+ tasks but per|=1|+orm w|=1|+ll i|=1|+ the pro|=1|+essing and size limitations of the [[PDP%2D11]]'s hardware.%0AHis approach to the problem resulted from collaboration also with ind|=2|+iduals at Bell Labs including [[Alfr|=1|+d Aho]], [[Elliot Pinson]], [[Jeffrey Ullman]], and [[Harold S. Stone]].%0A%0AIn the context of Unix, the use of the <tt>[[ed (Unix)%7Ced]]</tt> line editor provided diff with the natural ability to create machine%2Dusable "edit scripts"|=5|+se edit scripts, when saved to a file, can, along with the|=8|+l file, be reconstituted by <tt>ed</tt> in|=2|+ the modified file in its enti|=1|+ety.%0AThis|=1|+greatly reduced the [[secondary storage]] necessary to ma|=1|+ntain multiple version|=2|-1|+of a fi|=2|+.%0AMcIlroy considered writing a post%2Dprocessor for diff where a variety of output formats could be designed and implemented, but he found it more frugal and simpler to have diff be responsible for generating the synta|=2|-1|+and reverse%2Dorder input accepted by the <tt>ed</tt> command. In 1985, [[Larry W|=1|+ll]] |=1|-1|+omposed |=1|+ separat|=2|+utility, [[p|=1|+tch (U|=1|+ix)%7Cpatch]], that generalize|=2|+and extended t|=3|+ability to modify files wi|=2|+ diff |=2|+tput.%0AModes in [[Emacs]] also allow for convertin|=1|+ t|=1|+e forma|=5|+pa|=1|+c|=1|+es and even ed|=1|+ting patche|=1|+ interactively.%0A%0AIn|=2|+iff's early years, common |=1|+ses included compa|=5|+ch|=1|+nges in the|=2|-1|+ourc|=1|+ of softwar|=1|+ code and marku|=2|+f|=1|+r technical documents, |=3|+ifying|=1|+progr|=1|+m debugging ou|=1|+put,|=1|+comp|=1|+ring|=2|+ilesystem listings and analyzing compute|=1|+ assembly code.%0AThe output targeted for <tt>ed</tt> was mot|=1|+vat|=1|+d to provide compressio|=1|+ for a sequence of mo|=1|+ification|=2|+made to a file.%0AT|=1|+e [[SCCS%7CS|=2|+rce Code Control Sy|=1|+t|=1|+m]] (SCCS) emerged|=4|+the late 1970s as a |=1|+ir|=2|+t cons|=1|+quence of this develop|=1|-1|+ent.%0A%0AA conceptual pred|=1|+cesso|=5|-3|+diff includes [[Project Xanadu]], a hypertext project established in 19|=1|-2|+0 that had envisioned a versi|=1|+n |=1|+racking system necessary for its "transpointing windows" feature.%0AT|=2|+ featu|=1|+e subsumed|=1|+file differences in the expansi|=1|+e term "[[tr|=1|+nsclusion]]", whe|=1|+e a document has included in |=1|+t p|=1|+r|=1|+s of other documents or revis|=4|+.%0A%0AIn|=1|+the digit|=1|+l |=2|+alm|=1|+of the humanities, com|=1|+uter c|=1|+mpa|=1|+ison sys|=1|+ems were understood to have been created for working on |=1|+iterar|=2|+works publishe|=1|+ as large volumes.{{huh}}{{Fact%7Cdate%3DMarch 2007}}%0A%0A%3D%3D Usage %3D%3D%0A%0AIt |=1|+s invoked |=1|+rom the command line with the names o|=1|-1|+ two|=2|+iles: <tt>diff ''original''  ''new''</tt>.%0AThe o|=1|+tput of the |=1|+ommand represents the changes required to ma|=1|+e the ''orig|=2|+al'' file become the ''new'' file.%0A%0AIf ''ori|=1|+inal'' and ''new'' are directories, then|=5|+ will be run on each file that exists in both directories.%0AAn option|=2|+<tt>%2Dr</tt>, will d|=1|+scend any ma|=2|-1|+hing subdirectories to compare files between directories|=2|-1|+%0AAn|=2|+of |=4|+examples in the article use the follo|=1|+ing two files,  ''origin|=1|+l'' and ''new'':%0A%0A{%7C class%3D"prett|=1|+table"%0A%7C%2D|=1|+v|=2|+ign%3D"top"%0A%7C%0A''original'':%0A%0A  This part of th|=1|-1|+%0A|=1|+ docu|=1|+ent h|=1|+s stayed the%0A  same from version to%0A  version.  It shouldn't%0A  be shown if it doesn't%0A  |=1|+hange.  Othe|=1|+wise, th|=1|+t%0A  would not b|=2|+helping to%0A  comp|=1|+ess the size of the%0A  changes.%0A  %0A  This paragraph contains%0A  text that is o|=1|+tdated.%0A  It will be de|=2|+ted in the%0A  near future.%0A  %0A  It i|=2|+important to spell%0A  check this dokument. On%0A  the other hand, a%0A  misspelled word isn't%0A  the end of |=b|-2|+  Nothing in the|=1|-1|+re|=1|+t of%0A  this par|=2|+raph needs to%0A  be changed. Things can%0A  b|=2|-2|+added after it.%0A%7C %0A''new'':|=2|+  |=8|-1|+an important%0A  notice! It |=1|+hould%0A  therefore be locat|=3|-1|+at%0A  t|=2|+ begi|=1|+ning of|=3|+is%0A  docum|=1|+nt!%0A  %0A  This pa|=1|+t of th|=1|+%0A |=1|-1|+document ha|=3|+tayed the%0A  same fr|=2|+ v|=1|+rsi|=2|+ to%0A  v|=1|+rsion.|=1|-1|+ It sh|=2|+ldn't%0A  be|=1|+shown if it doesn't%0A  change.  Othe|=1|+wis|=1|+, th|=1|+t%0A  wou|=1|+d not be he|=1|+ping to%0A  compress an|=1|+thing.%0A  %0A  It is important to spell%0A  check this document. On%0A  the other|=3|+nd, a%0A  misspelled word isn'|=1|+%0A  th|=2|+end of the world.%0A  Nothing in the rest of%0A  this p|=1|+ragraph |=1|+ee|=1|+s to%0A |=1|+be changed. Things can%0A  be added a|=1|+t|=1|+r it.%0A  %0A  This paragraph contains%0A  important n|=1|+w additions%0A  to this document.%0A%7C}%0A%0AThe command <tt>diff origina|=2|+new</tt> produces the fol|=1|+ow|=1|-2|+ng ''normal|=1|+d|=1|+ff output'':%0A%0A  0a1,6%0A  > This is a|=1|+ important%0A  > notice! It |=1|+ho|=2|+d%0A  > |=1|+herefore be located at%0A  > the beginn|=4|+of |=2|+is%0A  > docum|=1|+nt!%0A  >%0A  8,14c14%0A  < co|=1|+press the size of the%0A  < changes|=2|+  <%0A  < This paragraph contains%0A  < text |=2|+at |=3|+outda|=2|+d.%0A  < It will be deleted in the%0A  < nea|=1|+ future.%0A  %2D%2D%2D%0A  > co|=1|+press|=1|+anything.%0A  17c17%0A  < check th|=3|+dokument. On%0A  %2D%2D%2D%0A  > check this document. On%0A  24|=1|+25,28%0A  >%0A |=1|+> This pa|=1|+agraph contains%0A  > important n|=1|+w additions%0A  > to this document.%0A%0AIn this traditional out|=1|+ut format, '''a''' stands for ''added'', '''d''' for ''de|=1|+eted'' |=1|+nd '''c''' for ''|=1|+hang|=1|+d''.%0ALine nu|=1|+b|=1|+rs of the origi|=1|+al file appear before a/d/c and |=1|+hose|=1|+o|=1|+ the m|=1|+dified file appea|=2|-2|+after.%0A[[Angle bra|=2|+et]]s|=1|-1|+appear at the beginning |=1|-1|+f lines that are added, deleted|=4|-1|+changed.%0AAdditi|=1|-1|+n lines a|=1|+e|=2|+dded|=1|+to t|=1|+e |=1|+riginal file to appear in the new file. Deletion lines are deleted from the original file to be missing in the new fil|=3|+%0AB|=1|+ default, lines c|=1|+mmon to both files are not shown.%0ALines that have moved will show |=1|+p|=1|+as added on their new location and as deleted on their old location.%0A%0A%3D%3D Variations %3D%3D%0A%0AMost diff implementations remain o|=1|+twardly unchanged |=1|+inc|=2|+1975.%0AThe modif|=1|+ca|=1|+ions|=1|+inc|=1|+ude |=1|-1|+mprovements to the core algorithm, th|=2|+addition of useful features to the command, and the design of ne|=1|+ output formats. T|=2|+ basic algorithm is described i|=2|-1|+the papers ''An O(ND) Difference Alg|=1|+rithm and its Variations'' by E|=1|+gene|=1|+W. Myers and in ''A File Comparison Program'' by Webb Miller and Myers.%0AThe algorithm was independently dis|=1|+overed |=1|+nd described in ''A|=1|+gorithms for Approximate String Matching'', by [[E. Ukkonen]].%0AThe first editions of the diff program were designed for |=1|+ine|=1|+compari|=2|+ns of text files expecting the [[newline]] character to deli|=1|+it lines.%0ABy th|=1|+ 1980s, supp|=1|+rt for bi|=1|+ary fil|=1|+s resulted in|=3|+shift i|=1|+ the |=1|+pplication's design and imple|=2|+ntation|=2d31|
